---
source: tests/cli/search.rs
expression: text(&output.stdout)?
---
find datasets on hugging face, kaggle and zenodo

usage: fetchloom search [options] <words>...

examples:
  fetchloom search iris
  fetchloom search fashion mnist
  fetchloom search iris --source kaggle,zenodo --limit 5
  fetchloom search iris --json

arguments:
  <words>...  dataset names or keywords, with or without quotes

options:
      --source <source>  search only this site: hf, kaggle or zenodo. repeat it
                         or use commas for more [possible values: hf, kaggle,
                         zenodo]
      --limit <n>        keep up to this many matches from each site, 1 to 20
                         [default: 3]
  -q, --quiet            print only the answer, warnings and errors
  -v, --verbose...       say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug
                         logs
      --json             print one JSON document on stdout, not the usual output
      --progress         with --json, keep plain progress lines on stderr
      --offline          use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes              answer yes to questions, but never pick a dataset for
                         you
      --color <when>     when to use color: auto, the default, always or never
  -C <dir>               run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
      --mirror <url>     ask the mirror at this web address or folder for files
                         before their sources. repeat it for more
  -h, --help             print help

on disk: nothing. prints the exact reference of each match, such as
zenodo:3608990, and downloads nothing

docs: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom/user/commands/search.html
